# Vercel Web Analytics Installation Report

## Summary
Successfully installed and configured Vercel Web Analytics for the Knotten Next.js project following the latest official documentation from https://vercel.com/docs/analytics/quickstart.

## Changes Made

### 1. Package Installation
- Installed `@vercel/analytics` package (version as specified by latest npm registry)
- Updated `package.json` with the new dependency
- Generated updated `package-lock.json` with dependency tree

### 2. Analytics Component Integration
Added the `<Analytics />` component from `@vercel/analytics/next` to all layout files to ensure complete coverage across the entire site:

#### Modified Files:

**`src/app/(moderne)/[locale]/layout.tsx`**
- Added import: `import { Analytics } from "@vercel/analytics/next";`
- Placed `<Analytics />` component at the end of the `<body>` tag
- Covers the modern design pages in both Norwegian (`/no`) and English (`/en`)

**`src/components/klassisk/Shell.tsx`**
- Added import: `import { Analytics } from "@vercel/analytics/next";`
- Placed `<Analytics />` component at the end of the `<body>` tag
- Covers the classic design pages (both Norwegian and English variants)
- This component is used by both `(klassisk)/layout.tsx` and `(klassisk-en)/layout.tsx`

**`src/app/global-not-found.tsx`**
- Added import: `import { Analytics } from "@vercel/analytics/next";`
- Placed `<Analytics />` component at the end of the `<body>` tag
- Ensures 404 pages are tracked

**`src/app/global-error.tsx`**
- Added import: `import { Analytics } from "@vercel/analytics/next";`
- Placed `<Analytics />` component at the end of the `<body>` tag
- Ensures error pages are tracked

## Implementation Details

### Framework-Specific Configuration
This project uses Next.js 16.4.6 with the App Router, and the implementation follows the official Vercel documentation for Next.js App Router projects:

1. Installed the package using npm (the project's package manager)
2. Imported the Analytics component from `@vercel/analytics/next`
3. Added the component to all root-level HTML layouts in the project

### Analytics Coverage
The Analytics component is now active on:
- ✅ All modern design pages (`(moderne)` route group)
- ✅ All classic design pages (`(klassisk)` and `(klassisk-en)` route groups)
- ✅ 404 Not Found pages
- ✅ Global error pages
- ✅ Both Norwegian and English language variants
- ✅ Portal pages (through the moderne layout)

### Build Verification
- ✅ Build completed successfully (`npm run build`)
- ✅ TypeScript compilation passed without errors
- ✅ All 275 static pages generated successfully
- ✅ Linter ran without errors (`npm run lint`)
- ✅ No test failures (no test suite configured)

## Next Steps
To activate analytics data collection:
1. Deploy this code to Vercel
2. Navigate to your Vercel project dashboard
3. Select "Analytics" from the sidebar
4. Click "Enable" to activate analytics tracking
5. After deployment, verify tracking by checking browser Network tab for requests to `/_vercel/insights/*`

## Notes
- Analytics tracking will only work when deployed to Vercel
- The component is lightweight and uses Next.js-optimized code splitting
- Analytics data will be available in the Vercel dashboard after user visits accumulate
- No environment variables or additional configuration required
